  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Hunters in the middle – pass past",
  "description": "Mark an area across the ice with cones. The players pair up with one ball per pair and line up on one side. One pair puts their ball aside and stands in the middle – they are the hunters.\n\nOn the signal every pair has to get across to the other side with their ball. The pairs pass to each other to get past the hunters, who try to win the ball or poke it out of the area. A pair that loses the ball fetches it, puts it aside and become hunters too. Then everyone skates back, and so on until only one pair still has a ball. They win the round and start as hunters in the next.\n\nHunters may only play the ball: stick low, no hitting sticks or legs. Variant: with an odd number, one player skates alone with a ball and may pass to any pair. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass when the hunter commits to the ball carrier – not too early, not too late."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Without the ball: skate into free ice beside or just ahead of the ball carrier, so the pass goes past the hunter."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Head up and the ball close to the stick when a hunter comes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Hunters: work together, close the passing lane and only play the ball with the stick low."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
